Well, maybe. But I think Orwell just did what he wanted to do, Dominic. If he fancied going to Spain to fight, off he went. If he wanted to go to Wigan, he went to Wigan. If he wanted to live in a bedsit, he lived in a bedsit. He just did it. And there's no sign of his politics in Eton, so I don't think he's going to be anti-imperialist. He wrote a couple of pretty bad poems in favour of the war. He's only a school boy, of course. Mind you, having said that, he's already writing pretty amusing things for the Election Times, which is Eton's newspaper. Pretty good, pretty funny. So he's talented. He has an imperial tradition in the family. I think the prospect of the university
嗯，也许吧。但我认为奥威尔只是做了他想做的事，多米尼克。如果他想去西班牙打仗，他就去了。如果他想去威根，他就去了威根。如果他想住单间公寓，他就住了。他就是这么做了。他在伊顿没有任何政治倾向的迹象，所以我认为他当时不会是反帝国主义者。他写了几首相当糟糕的诗来支持战争。当然，他当时只是个学生。话虽如此，他已经在为《伊顿公学时报》（Eton College Chronicle）写一些相当有趣的东西了。相当不错，相当有趣。所以他很有才华。他家族有帝国传统。我认为大学的前景

