was university. I think what happens is when you go to total institutions, it's easier. You find it easier if you have a known persona. And I think he found that at public school, and I think he was seeking to find it too in the empire, as well as all that romance and excitement that the empire, believe it or not, for boys of that type at that time, beckoned. Yeah. Just before we leave Eton, he was taught by Aldous Huxley at Eton, wasn't he? Which is, given the two great prophets, dystopian prophets of the 20th century, that is the most amazing coincidence.
是大学。我认为发生的事情是，当你进入全封闭机构时，这更容易。如果你有一个已知的角色，你会觉得更容易。我认为他在公学发现了这一点，我也认为他在帝国中也在寻求这一点，以及帝国所带来的所有浪漫和兴奋，信不信由你，对于当时那种类型的男孩来说，确实在召唤。是的。在我们离开伊顿之前，他曾由奥尔德斯·赫胥黎在伊顿教过，对吧？考虑到20世纪两位伟大的反乌托邦先知，这真是最令人惊奇的巧合。

