00:15:21.000 --> 00:16:03.000
Or is he self-mythologizing? There's a lot of argument, Tom, about that essay. Did he really shoot an elephant? Or is it a complete metaphor for the empire that is a dying elephant? Or is it a bit of each? Really hard to tell. I don't think we should really worry about it. Like so much of Orwell, I think he's better at the essays than he is at the novels. And this is a stunning, stunning essay on, in a way, how for a young policeman like him, the empire bullies him rather than he bullies the empire. He doesn't want to shoot this elephant. He doesn't know how to shoot this elephant.
还是他在自我神话化？汤姆，关于那篇文章有很多争论。他真的射杀了一头大象吗？还是这完全是帝国作为一个垂死大象的隐喻？还是两者兼而有之？真的很难说。我不认为我们真的应该担心这个问题。像奥威尔的许多作品一样，我认为他在散文方面比在小说方面更好。这是一篇令人惊叹的、令人惊叹的文章，在某种程度上，对于像他这样的年轻警察来说，帝国欺负他，而不是他欺负帝国。他不想射杀这头大象。他不知道如何射杀这头大象。

26
00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:45.000
He has to send for the gun to shoot the elephant. But when he takes aim at the elephant, by the way, a very expensive piece of capital in the Burmese economy, an elephant, and the crowd want him to shoot the elephant. So he has to act like the white man has to act. He has to be brave and fearless and take the elephant down, although he doesn't want to do any of these things. So the point he's making is that the imperialist wears a mask. It's not really him. It's the things, the subject people expect him to be. Yeah, that he's the prisoner of their expectations, isn't he? He's their prisoner rather than they are his prisoner. And there's he's the prisoner of their expectations, isn't he? He's their prisoner
他不得不派人去拿枪来射杀大象。但当他瞄准大象时——顺便说一句，大象是缅甸经济中非常昂贵的资本——人群希望他射杀大象。所以他必须表现得像白人应该表现的那样。他必须勇敢、无畏，把大象打倒，尽管他不想做这些事。所以他提出的观点是，帝国主义者戴着面具。那不是真正的他。那是被统治的人民期望他成为的样子。是的，他是他们期望的囚徒，不是吗？他是他们的囚徒，而不是他们是他的囚徒。而且有

