00:16:45.000 --> 00:17:56.000
rather than they are his prisoner. And there's about 2000 of them, of course, compared to him on his own, and he's only about 22 or something. So it's a great essay in that sense. There aren't many things I used to get my students to read out aloud in class where they were visibly moved. But I've had students crying while reading that essay. The death of the elephant is really very moving, powerful stuff. He describes what the elephant feels to be shot and to die on its knees. And it's exactly the same descriptions he attaches to his own when he himself is? And this produces the famous essay, Shooting an Elephant, but also the essay, A Hanging, because he has to hang somebody, doesn't he? He's part of a little posse that lead this guy out. And again, hang him in front of a crowd.
大约2000人，当然，相比他一个人，而且他只有22岁左右。所以从这个意义上说，这是一篇伟大的文章。我过去常让学生在课堂上大声朗读的文章并不多，但他们会被明显地感动。我曾有学生在读那篇文章时流泪。大象的死亡确实非常感人，非常有力量。他描述了大象被射中并跪着死去时的感受。这和他自己在他自己是……时所附带的描述完全一样？这产生了著名的文章《射杀大象》，还有文章《绞刑》，因为他必须绞死某人，不是吗？他是带领这个家伙出去的一小队人马的一部分。再一次，在人群面前绞死他。

28
