Is it in front of a crowd, Rob? Well, no, not a crowd. Just a few policemen and officers in a prison yard. He comes back from Burma in 1927. I mean, he's 24 years old. He's only 24, and he's had two lifetimes, Eton College and Burma. He declares to his parents he wants to be a writer. I mean, you can just see the look on their faces. He may as well have said, I want to wear a tutu, really. A tea trick graph on Hus and Hazleton. So he comes back to England and we've got a question from GT Avelado who asks, what was wrong with the name Eric Arthur Blair?
是在人群面前吗，罗伯？嗯，不，不是人群。只是监狱院子里的几个警察和官员。他于1927年从缅甸回来。我的意思是，他24岁。他才24岁，就已经经历了两种人生，伊顿公学和缅甸。他向父母宣布他想成为一名作家。我的意思是，你可以看到他们脸上的表情。他真的还不如说，我想穿芭蕾舞短裙。所以他回到英国，我们收到了GT·阿韦拉多提出的一个问题，他问，埃里克·阿瑟·布莱尔这个名字有什么问题？

29
00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:56.000
Because it's when he comes back to England, isn't it, that he starts to adopt the pseudonym. So why George Orwell? What's wrong with the name he's got? Eric Blair. He adopts it around 1932, 1933. It becomes natural to him, actually, Tom. He ends up signing himself George.
因为当他回到英国时，他开始采用笔名，对吧？那么为什么是乔治·奥威尔？他原来的名字有什么问题？埃里克·布莱尔。他在1932年、1933年左右采用了这个名字。汤姆，这对他来说实际上变得很自然。他最终以乔治的名字签名。

30
00:18:56.000 --> 00:19:14.000
His wife ends up calling him George. But why? Well, we don't know, really. George, St. George, patron saint of England, perhaps? Well, you know, we can do that. We can say a cigar signifies something else. Yes. But the river, is it named after the River Orwell?
他的妻子最终也叫他乔治。但为什么？嗯，我们真的不知道。乔治，圣乔治，英国的守护神，也许？嗯，你知道，我们可以那样做。我们可以说雪茄象征着别的东西。是的。但那条河，它是以奥威尔河命名的吗？

