Well, the River Orwell's in Suffolk. His parents are in Suffolk. He loved, he was a great naturalist. He loved the countryside. It's a broad and slow-moving river, very nice image. Some people say he wasn't too keen on the Scots. Therefore, he didn't like the name Blair. Of course, Blair has all kinds of resonances in our own times. But anyway, he dropped it and he went on using both names, Eric Blair and George Orwell, without much thought, really interchangeable. And then he's sort of drifting around, isn't he? I mean, if you look at him, it's quite a long period after his comeback from Burma, when he's sort of tutoring
