and teaching and writing. And when you're young, you're impatient and you feel sort of time slipping away. And actually, he writes these novels in the 1930s that, I mean, frankly, we'll probably skip over them because they're not his best work and they're not much read now. I mean, some people love them, no doubt. But arguably, the book that then makes him is The Road to Wigan Pier. So that's early 1936, Britain in the grip of the Depression. And he goes up north and he writes.
和教书、写作。当你年轻时，你很急躁，你会觉得时间在流逝。实际上，他在20世纪30年代写了这些小说，我的意思是，坦率地说，我们可能会跳过它们，因为它们不是他最好的作品，现在也没人怎么读了。我的意思是，有些人无疑很喜欢它们。但可以说，让他成名的书是《通往威根码头之路》。所以那是1936年初，英国正处于大萧条的控制之下。他去了北方，他写道。

