I mean, it's been done already. J.B. Priestley had done it and he writes, I mean, it's been done already. J.B. Priestley had done it, English Journey, a few years earlier. But what is it about that book? I mean, the funny thing, I used to teach that book to my students and they could never get a handle on the fact that the first half was all trudging around mines and sort of working people's houses and saying how simultaneously poor they were, but also cozy and authentic. And then the second half is an attack on middle-class socialists. Well, we'll come to the attack on middle-class socialists. That's a subject after your own heart.
我的意思是，这已经有人做过了。J.B.普里斯特利几年前做过《英国之旅》。但那本书到底有什么特别之处？我的意思是，有趣的是，我过去常给我的学生教那本书，他们永远无法理解这样一个事实：前半部分全是跋涉在矿井和工人的房子里，说他们是多么贫穷，但同时又是多么舒适和真实。然后后半部分是对中产阶级社会主义者的攻击。嗯，我们会谈到对中产阶级社会主义者的攻击。那是一个你非常感兴趣的主题。

